Galactic Dan - relocatable assembly source
==========================================

galdan.s      GNU as source (-march=armv2a). ./build.sh reassembles it and checks
              the result is byte-identical to ../extracted/GalacticDan_8000,ff8.
regen.sh      regenerate galdan.s from the analysis (../ghidra/gen_asm.py).

What "relocatable" means here
-----------------------------
Everything position-dependent is symbolic, so code/data can grow or shrink:
  * branches, ADR, PC-relative LDR/STR           -> labels
  * literal offsets (ldr rX,lit ; add rY,pc,rX)  -> .word target - (L_use + 8)
  * workspace above the image (BSS, stack)        -> ws_XXXX = _image_end + n
  * tables of PC-relative offsets (object/handler dispatch, voice generators,
    string tables)                                -> .word target - base
The game has no absolute pointers in its data (checked at run time).

Limits the assembler enforces for you (you get an error, not a bad build):
  * PC-relative LDR/STR reach +-4095 bytes: a literal can't move further than
    that from its user.
  * ADR immediates must stay encodable.
Limits it can't enforce (commented in the source):
  * Duff's-device jumps into unrolled plotters use immediate offsets: don't
    edit inside the unrolled bodies.
  * sub_866c uses the *address* of the string "statusbar" as a number (a latent
    bug in the original), so moving that string changes a computed value.

How it was verified
-------------------
emu.py        minimal RISC OS around ../extracted/tools/arm2.py: file loading,
              VDU variables, sound stubs, TickerV/VSync/mouse events.
provtrack.py  runs the original and records every image word used as an offset
              relative to pc or a pc-derived address (-> dyn_*.json).
difftest.py   runs the original and a padded rebuild in lock-step; checks the
              PC stream, every memory address, SWI arguments, VDU output and
              screen memory, modulo the padding.

  ./regen.sh --pad=8080:24,97f4:44,13aa4:104,1ba38:84,22718:204,26968:14
  python3 difftest.py ../extracted/GalacticDan_8000,ff8 ../asm_shifted/GalacticDan,ff8 \
          8080:24,97f4:44,13aa4:104,1ba38:84,22718:204,26968:14 20e6

Scenario (emu.SCENARIO): click PLAY, press Space at the Sector 1 briefing,
play on; 20M instructions; ~33% of the reachable code executes.  Two
different padded layouts both run identically for the whole 20M.
